---
title: "Hot Tub Service Areas Around Salt Lake City"
breadcrumb: "Service Areas"
description: "Soakers serves Salt Lake City and the Wasatch Front from Midvale: hot tub sales, delivery, installation and repair. Drive times and local tips by city."
layout: base.njk
permalink: /service-areas/
---

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container text-center">
    <h1>Areas We Serve Around Salt Lake City</h1>
    <p>Hot tub and swim spa sales, delivery, installation and repair from our Midvale showroom</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <p>
          Our showroom at 6905 S State St in Midvale sits near the middle of the Salt Lake Valley, so most of the Wasatch Front is a short drive away.
          We sell and install Artesian, Nordic and TidalFit spas, and we repair every brand, whether or not you bought it from us.
          Pick your city below for local planning tips: elevation and winter, HOA and lot considerations, and how far you are from the showroom.
        </p>

        <h2>City guides</h2>
        <div class="row">
          {%- for c in collections.serviceAreas %}
          <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <div class="guide-card">
              <h3><a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.data.city }}</a></h3>
              <p class="mb-0">{{ c.data.lede }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        <h2>Distance from our showroom</h2>
        <!-- Data and sources: src/_data/serviceAreaTable.js -->
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>City</th><th>Distance</th><th>Typical drive</th><th>Elevation (city center)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for r in serviceAreaTable %}
            <tr>
              <td>{% if r.url %}<a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.city }}</a>{% else %}{{ r.city }}{% endif %}</td>
              <td>about {{ r.miles }} mi</td>
              <td>about {{ r.minutes }} min</td>
              <td>about {{ r.elevation.toLocaleString("en-US") }} ft</td>
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #777;">
          Drive estimates assume light traffic. Our showroom sits at about 4,370 ft, so higher cities like Cottonwood Heights, Herriman and Park City usually run colder in winter.
        </p>

        <h2>Also served</h2>
        <p>
          We also serve Midvale, Orem, Provo and the rest of the Wasatch Front. Don't see your city? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>. We likely serve your area too.
          See our <a href="/services/">repair and service page</a> for everything we do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="site-cta">
  <div class="container text-center">
    <h2 style="color: white; margin-bottom: 15px;">Visit the Midvale Showroom</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 18px; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 25px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">
      6905 S State St, Suite A &middot; Monday–Saturday, 10 AM–5 PM &middot; 801-838-SPAS
    </p>
    <div>
      <a href="/contact/" style="display: inline-block; background: white; color: #1168b7; margin: 5px; padding: 14px 30px 10px; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none;">Get Directions &amp; Contact</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "@id": "{{ meta.url }}{{ page.url }}#service",
  "name": "Hot tub and swim spa sales, installation and repair on the Wasatch Front",
  "serviceType": "Hot tub and swim spa sales, delivery, installation, repair and maintenance",
  "provider": { "@id": "{{ meta.url }}/#business" },
  "areaServed": [
    {%- for r in serviceAreaTable %}
    { "@type": "City", "name": {{ r.city | tojson | safe }} },
    {%- endfor %}
    { "@type": "City", "name": "Midvale" },
    { "@type": "City", "name": "Orem" },
    { "@type": "City", "name": "Provo" }
  ],
  "url": "{{ meta.url }}{{ page.url }}"
}
</script>
